venue per employee of $207K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 13%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $12K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $925 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Surgery Partners, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $3.5B market cap on $3.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +9% over the past three years and +13% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $196M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Goodwill represents 64% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value","sev":"red","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8840762988723773},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 52/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Healthcare peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 12% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"The Deal Behind Mizuho\u2019s Downgrade of Surgery Partners (SGRY)","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/deal-behind-mizuho-downgrade-surgery-211048170.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794604248.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.637,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"How (SGRY) Movements Inform Risk Allocation Models","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/9/How_SGRY_Movements_Inform_Risk_Allocation_Models_111326012602_1794594362.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794594362.0,"origi